        "lines": [
          "Bildad Speaks"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then Bildad the Shuhite replied:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Dominion and dread belong to him,",
          "the one who establishes harmony in his heights."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Can his troops be numbered?",
          "Does his light not shine on everyone?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "How can a human be justified before God?",
          "How can one born of woman be pure?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If even the moon does not shine",
          "and the stars are not pure in his sight,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "how much less a human, who is a maggot,",
          "a son of man, who is a worm!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
